# HMDFS mode readback must validate execution safety semantics.
id:                     E7002-draft-2301
trigger_tool:           chmod|stat|hmdfs|w3-controller|elf-signer
phase:                  target-prepare,signing,permission-validation
error_signature:        'chmod 0?750.*stat.*0?710|signed_owner_execute_missing|mode.*exact.*mismatch'
severity:               2
category:               ohos|hmdfs|permissions|signing|w3|semantic_validation
match_keywords:         HMDFS mode projection, chmod readback, owner execute, group write, other write, signed ELF, exact mode equality, target prepare
root_cause:             HMDFS can project a requested POSIX mode to a different readback value while
                        preserving the security properties required by the task. Requiring exact equality
                        with the requested mode confuses advisory group read bits with executable and
                        write-safety invariants, causing a valid signed target to fail before launch.
affected_scope:         OpenHarmony target preparation flows that chmod and then validate task-private
                        executables, signers, shared libraries, scripts, or runners on HMDFS-backed paths.
verification_cmd:       chmod the frozen task-private file; read stat -c %a in the owning target shell;
                        require owner execute and reject group/other write; record the exact observed mode;
                        execute the exact signed artifact once under the transaction contract
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           semantic-mode-invariant-validation
rec_description:        Treat the observed mode as authoritative evidence. Parse its three octal digits,
                        require the owner digit to include execute, and require group and other digits to
                        exclude write. Keep exact-mode equality only when every bit is a functional or
                        security requirement. Freeze the policy before launch and preserve the observed mode
                        in the PREPARED receipt.
rec_command:            "case \"$mode\" in [1357][0145][0145]) : ;; *) exit 1 ;; esac"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               controller
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      exact-mode-policy-with-capability-proof
fallback_description:   If a consumer truly requires group read, group execute, set-id, or another exact
                        bit, first prove that requirement and that HMDFS can represent it. Otherwise fail
                        before launch and move to a create-new successor; do not reinterpret the old run.
fallback_command:       Record requested and observed modes plus the required bit predicate, then fail closed.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          validation
forbid_1_pattern:       stat.*=.*(?:750|755).*exact
forbid_1_reason:        Exact equality rejects harmless HMDFS projection when only execution and non-writability matter.
forbid_1_consequence:   A valid signed artifact is discarded before launch and consumes unnecessary successors.
forbid_2_pattern:       chmod.*(?:succeeded|rc=0).*(?:permission|execution).*PASS
forbid_2_reason:        chmod success does not prove the readback mode or target execution contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   Owner execute may still be absent, or unsafe group/other write bits may remain unnoticed.
principles:             P007, P018, P020
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             E046
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
doc_file:               drafts/E7002-draft-2301.md
last_updated:           2026-09-05
source_event:           GLEW 2.3.1 W3 r003 HMDFS chmod 0750 projected to 0710; r004 accepted the safe projection and executed the signed ELF
